        "original_id": "59d86330-0c66-5bb7-8204-1eafc0f1b284",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ted Tetzlaff, David Siegel, Scott McGehee, Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, Cleo Moore\n- Films: Gambling House, The Deep End\n- Roles: cinematographer, film director, screenwriter, producer\n- Places: Los Angeles, California, Sausalito, California\n\nFacts:\n- Dale H. \"Ted\" Tetzlaff was born on 3 June 1903 in Los Angeles, California.\n- Ted Tetzlaff was a Hollywood cinematographer active in the 1930s and 1940s, and he received an Academy Award nomination.\n- Gambling House is a 1951 crime film noir directed by Ted Tetzlaff and starring Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, and Cleo Moore.\n- The Deep End is a 2001 American film written and directed by David Siegel and Scott McGehee.\n- David Siegel is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer who has a long-standing writing-directing-producing partnership with Scott McGehee.\n- Ted Tetzlaff died on 7 January 1995 in Sausalito, California.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
